      "writtenOn": "2024-01-26T01:36:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m inclined to keep the dex_preopt properties in `java_import`. A few reasons:\n\n1. `java_import` is generally a mirror of `java_library`, so it looks cleaner and is easier to understand if properties of `java_library` are reflected in `java_import` rather than somewhere else.\n\n2. We may add more dex_preopt properties in the future, in addition to `profile_guided`. The data structure of `prebuilt_sscp_fragment` won\u0027t look great if it\u0027s packed with all those properties taken from multiple `java_import`s.\n\n3. You may be able to get rid of `java_import`s because they do look like hooks for dexpreopt and hiddenapi, but you won\u0027t be able to get rid of `java_sdk_library_import`s because they serve the stubs that are used for building the framework. Therefore, the value of removing `java_import` looks low to me since all the complexity for prebuilt java libraries has to be kept anyway for the sake of `java_sdk_library_import`.",
